This supports retries, audit history, and reconciliation jobs when async AWS steps complete later than the user session. DataZone inventory/publish operations are inherently staged, so durable workflow state is important. [docs.aws.amazon](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datazone/latest/userguide/manually-start-data-source-run.html)

## Guardrails

Before publishing, the backend should verify:

- the source row is still mapped to the requesting publisher,
- the underlying Glue table still exists,
- the table is still LF-managed and shared to M,
- the SMUS project role still has required external-database Lake Formation permissions,
- there is no active published asset for the same source unless you intend re-publish/version update,
- required business metadata is present. [docs.aws.amazon](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker-unified-studio/latest/userguide/grant-access-to-glue-asset.html)

It is also wise to lock the `eligible_source_tables` row or enforce one active publication request per source table, so two users cannot publish the same source simultaneously. That is an application design choice, but it fits the “latest published version is active” model in DataZone. [docs.aws.amazon](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datazone/latest/userguide/publishing-data-asset.html)

## Preferred operating model

The most scalable model for you is:

- **Producer account** owns data creation.
- **Lake Formation share** makes a table eligible.
- **Management account** owns discovery cache and workflow.
- **SMUS/DataZone project inventory** is the staging area.
- **Catalog publication** is the final discoverability step for consumers. [docs.aws.amazon](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lake-formation/latest/dg/cross-account-permissions.html)

That maps cleanly to your requirement: publishers cannot create SMUS assets directly, but they can safely choose which of their Glue tables should become catalog assets, and consumers only discover the assets after backend publication. [docs.aws.amazon](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fr_fr/sagemaker-unified-studio/latest/userguide/publishing-data-asset.html)
